{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To start, you need to identify the requirements for your trip."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the process initiation and the first step of identifying requirements/starting planning. Paraphrase preserves behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n2",
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If you choose \"Select one way\", you can proceed with the process. However, if you choose \"Select return\", you can also continue with the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the trip type choice as sequential actions rather than a conditional branch. Under relaxed rules, re-typing a decision as actions that both allow progression is a behaviour-preserving MATCH."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5",
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After that, you will need to select the departure city and then the destination city."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly maps the two explicit city selection steps in sequence."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once you have chosen the destination city, you can proceed to select the class."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the class selection step with correct ordering."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the class is selected, you can then choose your seat."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the seat selection step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After selecting your seat, you will be prompted to enter the type and number of passengers."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the passenger information entry step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once you have entered this information, you can continue to the flight selection."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the flight selection step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, once you have completed the flight selection, the process will come to an end."
      ],
      "justification": "Maps the final completion action and the explicit process termination point."
    }
  ],
